---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import passConfig from '../data/pass-config.json';
const appUrl = passConfig.studentAppUrl.trim();
const campUrl = `${appUrl}${appUrl.includes('?') ? '&' : '?'}mode=checkin`;
---
<Base title="checklings" description="Your Pixel Camp, original Checkling and progress travel with your school PIN.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-8">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">your friend · your school camp</p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight">checklings<span class="text-accent">.</span></h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-xl leading-relaxed">Take your Checkling to Pixel Camp. Care for your party, follow four founder journeys, build keepsakes in the workshop and climb the friendly stump ladder.</p>
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">one PIN. the same friend.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">Open Daily Check-In with your school account and enter your usual PIN. Choose your class, then open Pixel Camp below your Checkling. Your camp saves privately and follows that PIN and class across devices.</p>
      <a class="mt-6 inline-flex rounded-lg bg-accent px-6 py-4 font-bold text-white" href={campUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">open my school camp ↗</a>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">Just visiting? Choose <strong>visit Checkling only</strong> on the PIN screen. It works outside class hours. For a first visit, hatch your Checkling before opening camp.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">new · the checkaverse</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl font-bold">ride the bus to town.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed">The Checkaverse is the big shared town where everyone online walks around at the same time. Find your classmates in the plaza, say hi with a phrase, visit each other's houses in the Neighborhood and send a challenge. No typing, no real names. You get a trainer name when you step off the bus.</p>
      <a class="mt-6 inline-flex rounded-lg bg-accent px-6 py-4 font-bold text-white" href="https://game.grant-desk.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ride the bus ↗</a>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">Walk with the arrow keys or tap where you want to go. Battles open soon.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"><h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">four friends. four stories.</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Grow Mochi’s garden, repair Bolt’s machine, map the stars with Zee and bring Ember’s lanterns home. Each journey has three chapters and choices you make together.</p></div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-line p-5"><h2 class="font-display text-xl font-bold">a camp you make.</h2><p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed">Gather fallen wood, stones and reeds. Build eight keepsakes, find sixteen curios and unlock six camp decorations. Rest is free, and your friends stay safe while you’re away.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed">Your original friend, name and earned homes stay with you. Official attendance and streaks appear in camp; playing earns game discoveries and camp goals. Record attendance through the usual check-in.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">Already played the earlier browser camp? Save a file from its Menu. In your school camp, choose Menu → Load a save file. Review it before loading. Your school companion’s identity and official school rewards are preserved.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">Wait for “Saved to school” before closing. If a save fails, retry or use Menu → Save to file. On a shared Chromebook, close camp and choose Done or Different student when finished.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
